{"base_rate":0.02403204272363151,"brier":0.019643925233644857,"bss":0.16246681106551164,"bss_hi":0.3683421156537597,"bss_lo":-0.2654092416087005,"chart":{"base":[93.2,68.9],"lead":"62,213.4 272,205.7 482,194.8 692,158.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.16 — higher than 24% of cities","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 17% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 12% → rained 10%"},"rel":"62,466 138,424"},"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.005754339118825103,"ess":439.9176129499901,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Mexicali</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Mexicali rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, and its stated probabilities are honest throughout.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (25%), believe about\n<b>23%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 749 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nEL CENTRO 2 SSW, 18.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.16, ranked 162 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(68&ndash;201) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>564</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>110</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">0 of 3 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Mexicali</b> <span class=\"muted\">Mexico</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">probabilities honest throughout</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.16</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>68&ndash;201\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>749 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Mexicali &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Mexicali\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 68.29818181818182,358.8363636363636 148.19920000000002,255.81333333333333 148.19920000000002,318.90666666666664 68.29818181818182,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"373.25233644859816\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"373.25233644859816\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,382.0 68.29818181818182,378.6909090909091 148.19920000000002,299.49333333333334\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 564 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 110 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.29818181818182\" cy=\"378.6909090909091\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"148.19920000000002\" cy=\"299.49333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(2%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Mexicali the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.41) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.30).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-1.297</td><td class='num'>4.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'>0.308</td><td class='num'>2.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>216</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>0.357</td><td class='num'>0.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>0.409</td><td class='num'>0.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":32.62781,"lon":-115.45446,"n":749,"n_cit